From: OMP Agent <agent@local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 05:40:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] F-SPLIT-1: remove dead split_of() seed-range heuristic

ScenarioTemplate.split_of() classified a relative seed by numeric range
(<1000 dev, <2000 validation, else holdout). It has zero callers on any
current generation path (verified by reference census and import sweep),
carries relative/absolute seed semantics inconsistent with the resolve_seed
split-offset model, and invites exactly the silent misclassification
F-SPLIT-1 closes: a caller reading split_of(1500) would conclude VALIDATION
while every live path resolves splits by explicit label.

Removal is its own reviewed change per the adjudication rule (dead-code
cleanup must not ride the fail-open correction). scripts/d6b_runner_fixed.py
still defines a local method of the same name inside a standalone historical
script class; it is unreachable from the canonical runtime and is left for
the historical-scripts review rather than silently edited here.

Known results at this commit:
  configured suite (testpaths=tests)   1218 passed, 0 failed
---
 src/arena/templates/base.py | 10 +---------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/arena/templates/base.py b/src/arena/templates/base.py
index 2ae68377f..415c73654 100644
--- a/src/arena/templates/base.py
+++ b/src/arena/templates/base.py
@@ -170,15 +170,7 @@ class ScenarioTemplate(ABC):
             Populated ArenaScenario.
         """
         ...
-    
-    def split_of(self, seed: int) -> ScenarioSplit:
-        """Determine which split a relative seed belongs to."""
-        if seed < 1000:
-            return ScenarioSplit.DEV
-        elif seed < 2000:
-            return ScenarioSplit.VALIDATION
-        else:
-            return ScenarioSplit.HOLDOUT
+
 
 
 def create_scenario_from_template(template: ScenarioTemplate, seed: int,
